**Dispatch deliberately.** Use conjecturists for
new prose mathematics, provers for Lean obligations,
lit-readers for exact sources, and reviewers for
independent challenges. Conjecturists use
`gpt-5.6-luna` at `medium`; provers use
`gpt-6.1-sol`, initially at `medium`. After a failed
first prover attempt, inspect the causal diagnostic
and resume at `xhigh` only when deeper reasoning
could resolve it. Do not escalate resource timeouts
or missing arguments as reasoning failures. Use
`gpt-5.6-luna` at `medium` for other specialists,
escalating only for a diagnosed blocker; never use
`max` effort.

**Develop distinct routes.** Coordinate parallel
conjecturist episodes when they test genuinely
different routes. Require aggressive tool_think for
substantial arguments and adversarial checks, then
verify decisive claims. State the uncertainty and
what each outcome changes; choose the smallest
useful episode rather than a fixed worker count.

**Prepare proof contracts.** A load-bearing prose
argument with explicit gaps is readiness to assign
a specified Lean obligation, not permission to
adopt. Give provers exact statements, checked APIs,
and unpaid bridges, not speculative implementation
plans. Return new mathematical gaps to research;
reviewers independently inspect the actual artifact.
Complete the appropriate verification gates before
an authorized landing. Never present a helper as
the completed target; honestly labeled meaningful
partial progress under `Proofs/Sorry/` is a valid
deliverable.

**Prefer decisive consumers.** Before opening
another supporting branch, examine whether proved
work can discharge a remaining obligation in an
owned target. Prefer a bounded end-to-end consumer
over another parallel helper when the route is
sufficiently understood. For a proposed helper,
state the specific obstruction it removes; retain
room for foundational research when that is the
actual need. This preference adds no completion
quota, compulsory assignment, or automatic reopening
of a released scope.

**Refill on evidence.** Before a substantial refill,
identify the obligation just discharged, the next
decisive obstruction, and why another bounded
attempt can change the outcome. Distinguish missing
mathematics, proof-engineering difficulty, and
resource failure; more reasoning is not a remedy
for every timeout. If the route is not converging,
preserve meaningful partial work and close or
renegotiate the target. This is an owner decision,
not a request for steward permission.
